{"study_accession":"PRJNA494155","secondary_study_accession":"SRP163027","title":"Differential analysis of gene expression profiles in peripheral blood cells of patients with cervical lesions","description":"Using RNA-sequencing analysis of peripheral blood cells from 11 cervical cancer patients, 21 cervical intraepithelial neoplasia patients and 19 healthy controls, we identified a group of differentially expressed genes. A real time quantitative reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction (qRT-PCR) was applied to the validation of candidate markers in the blood of 115 patients and 46 healthy controls. The results suggest that a six-gene predictor set (GZMB, NDUFA1, GPR84, NUAK1, AGAP1 and CIR1) can be used as candidate genes for the detection of cervical cancer. Overall design: The mRNA profiles of peripheral blood cells from 11 cervical cancer patients, 21 cervical intraepithelial neoplasia patients and 19 healthy control participants were sequenced using Illumina 2500.","pubmed":"32064895","geo_series":"","n_samples":51,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN10148583","study_accession":"PRJNA494155","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"cervical cancer 7","description":"cervical cancer 7","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3408352","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2018-10-05","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood cells"],["tissue","peripheral blood cells"],["disease","cervical cancer"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR7946341","experiment_accession":"SRX4780425","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":26722130,"base_count":8016639000,"first_public":"2018-10-05","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM3408352: cervical cancer 7 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN10148584","study_accession":"PRJNA494155","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"healthy control 19